@startuml UC-MG05-activity
' UC-MG05 Take over and handle a care exception, with the UC-SYS02 timeout escalation
' branch, as built at the end of Sprint 2. Source: use case specification v3.0, amended
' where the team decided otherwise (manager duty rosters are not modelled).
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng UC-MG05-activity.puml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #444444
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8F8F6
  BorderColor #9A9A9A
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #888888
  TitleFontStyle bold
}
title UC-MG05  Take over and handle a care exception\n(with UC-SYS02 automatic escalation on timeout)

|System|
start
:Exception recorded
(caregiver report, elder SOS,
or missed check-in);
:Tell everyone who could act, at once:
every manager, the family bound to the elder,
the caregiver who last visited;
note right
  Being told and being answerable are
  separate: the broadcast never waits
  for the chain.
end note
:Assemble the escalation chain **at runtime**:
assigned responder, then the manager who
handled this elder before, then any manager,
then family escalation;
note right
  The continuity level is left out for LOW
  severity. Manager duty rosters are not
  modelled, so time of day and who is on
  duty do not enter the chain.
end note
:Name the first responder and start the
response countdown (length set by severity);
|Manager|
:Named task on the exception queue,
with its countdown;

while (Taken over before the countdown expires?) is (no, timeout)
  |System|
  if (Next level on the chain?) then (yes)
    :UC-SYS02: hand over to the next level,
    tell the previous and the new responder,
    log the timeout and its reason,
    start the next level's countdown;
    note right
      The scan re-reads the incident first.
      If it was taken over in the meantime,
      the escalation is cancelled and the
      near miss is recorded (SYS02 2a).
    end note
  else (chain exhausted)
    :Mark UNRESOLVED_ESCALATED,
    pin it to the top of the queue,
    tell the family nobody took it on;
    stop
  endif
endwhile (yes)

|Manager|
:Take over: the countdown stops,
the workbench shows the incident,
its timeline and the escalation chain;
:Contact the family (phone, push or email);
|Family|
if (Reached?) then (yes)
  :Agree the response with the manager;
  |Manager|
  :Log the contact as REACHED;
else (not reached)
  |Manager|
  :Log the contact as NOT REACHED,
  with the reason;
  |System|
  :Offer the standard playbook
  for this category;
  |Manager|
  :Apply the playbook;
endif
:Carry out the response;
if (Situation changes?) then (yes)
  :Change the severity;
  |System|
  :Re-assemble the chain for the new severity,
  the timeline continues, no new incident;
  |Manager|
endif
:Record the outcome and close the incident
(only the manager handling it may);
|System|
:Every step, with its timestamp, is on the incident timeline
(refused take-overs and timed-out levels included);
stop
@enduml
